paragraphs:
LAERTES
A double blessing is a double grace;
chance smiles upon a second leave-taking.

GHOST
Murder most foul, as even the best of murders are;
but this one most foul, strange, and unnatural.

HAMLET
I'm sorry they offend you, heartily;
yes, truly, heartily.

GUILDENSTERN
Happy in that we're not too happy;
on Fortune's cap we're not the very button.

HAMLET
 Why, let the wounded deer go weep,
 the unhurt deer play;
 for some must watch, while some must sleep,
 so runs the world away.
Wouldn't this, sir, and a forest of feathers—if the rest of my fortunes turn against me—with two Provincial roses on my slashed shoes, get me a place in a company of players, sir?

KING
Arm yourselves, I pray you, for this speedy voyage;
for we will put fetters on this fear,
which now goes far too free.

HAMLET
You pray badly.
I beg you, take your fingers from my throat;
for though I am not hot-tempered and rash,
yet I have something dangerous in me
that your wisdom should fear. Off with your hand!

HAMLET
So much for this, sir. Now let me tell you the other;
you remember all the circumstances?

KING
I do not fear it. I have seen you both;
but since he has improved, we have the odds.

KING
Stay, give me drink. Hamlet, this pearl is yours;
here's to your health.
